From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: aiueo52 <aiueo52@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 19:43:42 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 027/105] w8a16 gemv: retune for the [N, K] weight layout the
 server actually passes

Fp8LinearMethod keeps the [N, K]-contiguous quantized weight, stores its [K, N]
transposed view on the layer, and transposes it back at the call site, so
w8a16_gemv always receives stride (K, 1). `_BY_SHAPE` assumed the opposite and
keyed every fp8 row contig_n=True, which no call matches: the server has been
running _plan's fallback tile ([32, 128], planner split count, 4 warps) for all
seven fp8 shapes. Only the two bf16 rows were keyed correctly and live.

Re-key the table to the true layout and add M-bucket overrides. M == 1 takes
the USE_DOT=False broadcast path on every shape measured (M_PAD drops 16 -> 1,
so both the accumulator and the split-K partials shrink 16-fold), and _plan's
fallback now emits a [128, 256] tile with 8 warps for shapes whose N alone
fills the machine.

bench/w8a16v2 is retooled to match and committed with it: shapes.py builds the
weights in the true layout and carries the in-server medians, the metric is now
the CUPTI kernel-duration median (what the serving torch profile reports) and
not graph-replay wall time, repro_w8a16v2.py gates the harness against the
in-server numbers before any tuning (worst fp8 row 21.7% low, every launch grid
identical), tune_v3.py runs the two-phase sweep, and verify_v3.py checks each
chosen config against an fp32 reference plus a bit-identical graph replay.

CUPTI medians over a >= 4x L2 working set, pre-v3 plan -> tuned:

  GDN in_proj_ba    96x2560 bf16  M=16   5.86 -> 2.62 us  2.23x
  draft lm_head  32768x2560 fp8   M=1   62.14 -> 52.93 us 1.17x
  shared gate_up  1280x2560 fp8   M=1    5.09 -> 4.13 us  1.23x
  shared down     2560x640 fp8    M=1    3.68 -> 3.07 us  1.20x
  MoE router       512x2560 bf16  M=1    4.16 -> 3.62 us  1.15x
  MTP fc          2560x2560 bf16  M=1   10.82 -> 10.21 us 1.06x
  attn qkv       13312x2560 fp8   M=16  24.83 -> 23.62 us 1.05x
  GDN in_proj_qkvz 16384x2560 fp8 M=16  29.66 -> 28.48 us 1.04x
  lm_head       248320x2560 fp8   M=16 407.10 -> 400.72 us 1.02x

Per decode step over the profiled call counts, primary shapes only:
W16 4.611 -> 4.223 ms (-8.4%), W4 3.325 -> 3.138 ms (-5.6%). No (shape, M)
row regresses.

The in_proj_ba entry contradicts the note it replaces ("split-K measured slower
in the server, 14.8 vs 9.4us"): here split-K is 2.2x faster and the ranking is
unchanged from a 1.9x-L2 to a 15x-L2 working set. Worth re-checking in a
serving profile.

